@Zachery Sutton I replaced with truncated French string - I suppose this looks alright. Not all languages would have an abbreviation that would fit (I can't think of one in French, at least).

As long as we keep the tooltip text and text read by screenreaders is the full string this should be fine.

We may want to specify a recommended max char limit for the Pontoon entry, but I suppose that's on eng to do.

@Zachery Sutton Couple of questions as I'm working on engineering ticket for this:
* are the codes static or interactive with hover/focus states?
* do we have mockups for hover/focus/active states for the download/copy/print buttons?

@Peter Benvenuto what is the expected timeout for this snackbar (if there is any)? At minimum, 20 sec  is needed since there would be only one essential action - to read and understand the message. Note: this may still be missed by users of magnification software, etc., so ideally it would not auto-disappear

Engineering note: 
* ensure the snackbar is announced to a screen reader, i.e. by using `role="alert"` on its container - this would allow not to force the focus placement on the message (since there is no action that the user is expected to take on it) but would ensure screen reader users would be hear it (be aware of this status). Not announcing it would create an S2 issue.

Alt subcopy: Enter the code that was sent to your recovery phone within 5 minutes.

-- this uses consistent language (recovery phone) instead of showing part of the phone number. just in case we are worried about showing last 4 digits of recovery phone to a bad actor. 

@Peter Benvenuto

